video-editor
============

This plugin is released under the MIT License (see LICENSE). It contains code adapted from two
MIT-licensed projects, whose licence texts are in LICENSES/:

- video-use (c) 2026 Browser Use, https://github.com/browser-use/video-use
  -> src/videoeditor/core/{render,pack,grade,timeline}.py, skills/manim-video/,
     tests/test_render_*.py
- clipify (c) 2026 Louise de Sadeleer, https://github.com/louisedesadeleer/clipify
  -> src/videoeditor/core/{moments,reframe}.py and the opus/karaoke/minimal caption styles
     in src/videoeditor/core/captions.py

Changes: ElevenLabs transcription replaced by local Whisper emitting the same JSON shape; macOS-only
flags and font paths removed; captions merged into one engine; the scripts became a package behind one
questionnaire-driven CLI.

`ve publish` is a from-scratch design that replaces the browser-automation approach of
profullstack/social-poster (MIT) with official platform APIs; none of its code is used.

Optional dependencies (installed by the user, never bundled; no source from them is in this plugin):

- whisperX (BSD-2-Clause), https://github.com/m-bain/whisperX            extra `speech-plus`
- Demucs (MIT, maintained fork), https://github.com/adefossez/demucs      extra `stems`
- Remotion (custom licence, https://www.remotion.pro/license)             npm packages used by
  src/videoeditor/templates/remotion_overlay, which is this plugin's own code and contains no Remotion
  source. Free for individuals, for-profit organisations of up to 3 people and non-profits; others need
  a company licence.
